gmusicbrowser (1.1.99.6) forky; urgency=low

  * Saved libraries now store filenames and cover paths as readable UTF-8, with
    `filenames=utf8` in the gmbrc header. Existing percent-escaped libraries are
    still read and are converted on the next save. Filenames containing invalid
    UTF-8 bytes retain a lossless escaped representation. Older releases do not
    understand the new format's literal percent signs; use a backup when downgrading.

 -- Carl di Ortus <reklamukibiras@gmail.com>  Fri, 06 Oct 2026 22:17:00 +0300
 
